  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 235 AM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nBy late Sunday and into Monday morning, a large upper low encroaches \nfrom the west and moisture pooling in from Mexico begins increasing \nrain chances over the western reaches of the region. Additional \nmoisture from what is now Hurricane Simon is slated to follow the \nsame path north through Mexico and stream across West Texas. Weak \nshortwave troughs ahead of the main low bring broad, but somewhat \nlow (10-40%) rain chances to the area for Tuesday and Wednesday. \nDetails remain sparse on just which areas will receive the most rain \nand how much as it is dependent on where the low over the western US \nis located as the moisture from Hurricane Simon moves into the area. \n\nDespite the better rain chances, highs will remain well above normal \nwith most locations in the 80s to low 90s. Overnight lows stay in \nthe 60s to low 70s. Thursday sees the low to the west move east into \nthe Plains and brings temperatures down to normal into the 70s and \n80s. Similar rain chances from Tuesday and Wednesday continue into \nThursday and Friday, but shift to the eastern and southern portions \nof the CWA. A cold front looks to move through the area on Thursday \nand brings the first batch of cooler air of the season. Highs in the \n70s with lows dipping into the 50s for most. \n\n-Stickney",
